		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4902&amp;p=35918#p35918"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Good job, as usual.<br><br>A question about roaming, my favorite feature <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"> :<br><br>It could be possible this scenario:<br><br>Switching on radio<br>GPS get fix<br>Radio compares actual position to nearest repeater position, as per repeater channel list, and switch to a proper repeater?<br>And in case of loosing position (e.g. moving to building or tunnel), when radio GPS hit again fix, switching to nearest repeater?<br>Thanks for patience <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"></div></blockquote>But it works like this, minus the fact that the firmware don't care about GPS fix losing, but a GPS fix is mandatory to perform continuous zone sorting.<br><br>You're defining a Roaming distance (5/10/20km), so if the last position where the channel list was sorted exceeds this distance, a new sort is performed, and the closest channel is selected.</div></blockquote>Ok, right. I mean that combining distance with gpx fix and, maybe, RSSI (a repeater can be the nearest but not the strongest, due to antenna orientation, etc...) could be fantastic, mainly for GPS poor performance in RT3S, for example.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=558">IK1HJT</a> — Tue Feb 25, 2025 9:53 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
