<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Good job, as usual.<br><br>A question about roaming, my favorite feature <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"> :<br><br>It could be possible this scenario:<br><br>Switching on radio<br>GPS get fix<br>Radio compares actual position to nearest repeater position, as per repeater channel list, and switch to a proper repeater?<br>And in case of loosing position (e.g. moving to building or tunnel), when radio GPS hit again fix, switching to nearest repeater?<br>Thanks for patience <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"></div></blockquote>But it works like this, minus the fact that the firmware don't care about GPS fix losing, but a GPS fix is mandatory to perform continuous zone sorting.<br><br>You're defining a Roaming distance (5/10/20km), so if the last position where the channel list was sorted exceeds this distance, a new sort is performed, and the closest channel is selected.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Tue Feb 25, 2025 4:54 am</p><hr />
